From 35a7be2203cef93354c1f16d0201ffd0f7ba3e94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:19:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] The next fight on a player's map opens framed, and a map
 taken off the page stops listening

Two causes, one implicit machine. The map's life on the page was loose lets in map.js: `fitted` held the grid's size as
what was framed, so a new fight on the same ground counted as framed and opened at the last fight's zoom, with the last
fight's gesture, choice, brush and last draw kept; and nothing told a map that its screen replaced its box, so each
map left behind kept the window's resize, its hotbar observer and its news line. The life is now a machine of core,
src/core/combat/map-mount.ts (blank, opening a fight, framed, gone; its TABLE, chart and MACHINES entry): a fight is its
id (MapSource.input names it), a new one forgets the last and frames afresh, a resize while the frame is hidden frames
it again when it shows, and `gone` stops every listener. map.js feeds it each draw, the resize and `destroy`, which
combat.js and table.js call where they replace the map's box. A lint holds that a view that mounts the map destroys it.
Audit BUG-views-8 and SM-views-3; held by the two map cases of tests/e2e/battle-map.e2e.ts and tests/map-mount.test.ts.
